{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1364081-\u200bother-2e-books","id":1364081,"title":"\u200bOther 2e books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-29T18:47:09-08:00","id":1364081,"title":"\u200bOther 2e books","content":"Hello folks,<br /> <br /> I am really getting into Mage 2e. I got \u2018Signs and Sorcery\u2019 and the \u2018Chronicles of Darkness\u2019 but am also looking forward to the new antagonist book coming out on the horizon.<br /> Out of the other 2e books which ones have you found enhance your games? I personally am getting Geist (because I love sin-eaters) and I am sure it will help with a lot of ghost stuff. I assume werewolf is equally as helpful for spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T18:56:14-08:00","id":1364082,"title":"","content":"Werewolf is fantastic for spirits!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T19:24:28-08:00","id":1364083,"title":"","content":"I liked all of the Dark Eras books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T19:41:13-08:00","id":1364086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1364081-\u200bother-2e-books?p=1364082#post1364082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf is fantastic for spirits!</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1364081-\u200bother-2e-books?p=1364083#post1364083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked all of the Dark Eras books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these are truth. Pretty much any of the core books have plenty of cannon (and canon) fodder that could be turned into mysteries for Mages. I'd also suggest checking out the Night Horrors line, particularly <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282275/Night-Horrors-Shunned-by-the-Moon?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Shunned by the Moon</a> and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/236133/Night-Horrors-Enemy-Action?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Enemy Action</a>. The 1e Night Horrors books are also fairly easy to convert and many of them are quite good. Beast is often divisive but the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/236135/Beast-Players-Guide?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Beast Player's Guide</a> is excellent and expands a bit on the Astral and how Beasts fit in there. It was also written by DaveB, so it reads very similar to the cosmological aspects of Signs of Sorcery. <br /> <br /> And back the Hunter Kickstarter next week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T21:00:27-08:00","id":1364095,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the number one recommendation I can make from a practical standpoint? The Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook. While unlike First Edition, Second Edition games (aside from odd-man-out Demon) don't require it in any way, it contains two big elements of use: Horrors, a system for miscellaneous unconnected supernatural creatures and beings, and the God-Machine Chronicle, which includes a series of modular adventure hooks that are very flavorful and weird. Mage games thrive on having mysteries to poke your nose into, and these make for great starting points.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras (the first one, not the Companion or Dark Eras 2) contains two era writeups which, in addition to being fascinating and playable on their own, help illuminate the standpoint of Mage games set in later periods: the Sundered World, which explores a time-fractured period when the Shadow Realm was contiguous with the material world, and To the Strongest, which explores the foundational philosophies of mages of antiquity which later contributed to the beliefs of the Orders.<br /> <br /> Less practically, but high in quality: Demon: the Descent remains my #1 favorite CofD corebook of either edition, which is an impressive feat alongside Changeling First Edition and Mage Second. Its flavor is rather particular to the game, but angels and demons wield reality-warping powers that can occasionally engage with mages on their level. The Storyteller's Guide supplement has a section that briefly covers their relationship with mages and the Seers of the Throne in particular: a mysterious alliance wherein angels of the God-Machine occasionally emerge to assist pylons, or pylons receive mystery commands to aid what turns out to be a God-Machine project, though the Seers caught in the middle do not understand why.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in games which incorporate power-mad sorcerers willing to experiment on their fellow humans in the pursuit of power, keep an eye out for the general publication of Deviant: the Renegades, which is very easy to raid for crossover NPCs while still remaining in the theme of other gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T04:40:08-08:00","id":1364135,"title":"","content":"The Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook is the big one. Has all the systems you need for modularity of gameplay, and helps to tie everything back into the core themes of the franchise.<br /> <br /> If you're doing anything with an eye on violence, get Hurt Locker. I mean, honestly, you should just get that anyways.<br /> <br /> Everyone else has given solid advice and it's worth backing (though no one mention Changeling: the Lost for their other world yet?), but really beyond that it comes down to the major themes and moods you want to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T22:55:01-08:00","id":1364477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1364081-\u200bother-2e-books?p=1364083#post1364083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked all of the Dark Eras books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting! I see there are two sections: The Sundered World &amp;To the Strongest. What bits inspired you or that you found usable for your game?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T23:12:05-08:00","id":1364479,"title":"","content":"Thanks all, I will look into getting at least the pdf of some of those books. I probably will end up GMing mage here in a few months so I am trying to gather up resources so that the players can get the most out of their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T23:22:31-08:00","id":1364480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1364081-\u200bother-2e-books?p=1364477#post1364477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting! I see there are two sections: The Sundered World &amp;To the Strongest. What bits inspired you or that you found usable for your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sundered Woeld is set in the Neolithic Era during the Vinca civilization, and contextualize how no matter how far back you go there is always a \u201clost civilization\u201d in the Awakened\u2019s \u201cpast\u201d. Strange animistic gods with material form called Pangeans walk the spirit wilds between the mortal world and spirit world, and their hearts create Demesnes.<br /> <br /> To the Strongest is set at the death of Alexander the Great and shows how the Diamond Orders arose from the cultural crossroads of Hellenic, Indian, Persian, and Egyptian civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}